OB_section.md
   1: ### 2026-10-18 -- `fableheldform`: seventeen walled Fable entries carry a stage token; nine rows that shut while a stage awaited Fable go back to held; the wider class is filed
   2: 
   3: * **`fableheldform` (MED) HELD for fable5** -- the conversion is done.  Under the owner's 2026-10-17 directive a Fable
   4:   wall is a SEAT FAILURE recorded as a HELD marker with a question, never agreement; seventeen entries had recorded one
   5:   in untokened prose, which `stage_tokens.is_answer()` counts as an answer.  Fifteen now carry the HELD token (prose and
   6:   receipt kept); `cxlaunchquotation`'s 2026-10-16 v2 wall and its V3 wall carry the non-answer token instead, because a
   7:   later pass superseded each and Fable answered that one (V4, 2026-10-17).  No same-day answer can clear a HELD tag on V3
   8:   under the strictly-later discharge rule (a later-date one could), and one on the v2 wall would already be cleared
   9:   by V4 (Grok 4.7, corrected by GPT-6 Astra's confirm).  Design pass 1 (`regress/artifacts/fableheldform/
  10:   design_20261018/`): GPT-6 Astra, Grok 4.7 and GLM 5.3 all chose this (option A); Fable 5.1 walled, so this row's own
  11:   review is held.
  12: * **NINE ROWS REOPENED, `closed` -> `held`**: `sgirekills`, `sgirandomcolour`, `mapledmaaddr`, `xscaleinten`,
  13:   `ppcrldimimask`, `ppcrlwimiwidth`, `ppcgateimageskip`, `cxlaunchquotation`, `dashokclass`.  Each was shut on 2026-10-17
  14:   or 2026-10-18 while its review stage (and `sgirekills`' research stage) held a Fable wall written as an untokened
  15:   note; a row may not close while a stage awaits a seat (`check_stage_panels.py`, CLOSED-WHILE-HELD), so with the token
  16:   in place each is held until Fable answers.  Each keeps its closure object (the record of that close), names in
  17:   `reopened` every commit whose subject called it closed (section L), heads its state note with the warrant, and adds to
  18:   its `hold_question` the packet of the pass Fable walled on.  GPT-6 Astra's confirm on `ip30abortkill` earlier the same
  19:   afternoon is the precedent.  **The owner question the panel named** -- may a row close while its research or review
  20:   question is held for Fable (a change to section H and the state semantics)? -- is in `fableheldform`'s
  21:   `hold_question`; until it is answered, rulings and commits proceed and closes wait.
  22: * **`wiringcliff`** -- `#565`'s two Fable stages (pass 1, pass 2 + F2) carry the HELD token and their question.
  23: * **`untokenedanswers` (MED, open)** -- the same defect for every seat and date.  A keyword correlate finds 497 matches
  24:   among entries counted as answers, on 129 rows, 81 of them closed -- actual non-answers and known false positives
  25:   together -- among them deliberate roster exclusions that section H's nine-seat count reads as seats that answered:
  26:   `ppcgateimageskip`'s review is 9/9 only through seven untokened non-answers (five owner-roster exclusions, GLM
  27:   deliberately not fired for that records question, Fable held after its wall).  Owed: GLM 5.3's keyword-free review of
  28:   every counted Fable entry (the keyword census is reconnaissance, not that review), a forward-only structural check
  29:   that reds a NEW untokened non-answer, an owner ruling on how an excluded seat is recorded, and row-by-row correction
  30:   of the history when a round touches it (no sweep).
CHANGELOG_block.md
   1: # Records, 2026-10-18: `fableheldform` -- seventeen walled Fable entries carry a stage token; nine rows that shut while a stage awaited Fable go back to held; the wider class is filed
   2: 
   3: **The defect** (filed by `#566`).  The owner's 2026-10-17 directive records a Fable wall as a SEAT FAILURE with a HELD
   4: marker and a question, never as agreement.  Seventeen `fable5` entries since 2026-10-16 recorded one in untokened prose
   5: ("NOT FIRED", "SEAT FAILURE", "HTTP 429"), and `stage_tokens.is_answer()` counts any untokened entry as an answer -- so
   6: the checkers read Fable as having answered, and nine rows passed section H's no-close-while-held rule and were shut on
   7: 2026-10-17 and 2026-10-18 with a Fable stage still owed.  GPT-6 Astra's confirm on `ip30abortkill`'s closure records
   8: (`d42c76a8`, the same afternoon) is what exposed it: a review stage then reads complete on older answers.
   9: 
  10: **What this commit does** (records only):
  11: * tags fifteen walls with the HELD token, keeping each entry's prose and receipt, and `cxlaunchquotation`'s 2026-10-16
  12:   v2 and V3 walls with the non-answer token instead -- a later pass superseded each and Fable answered that one (V4,
  13:   2026-10-17); no same-day answer can clear a HELD tag on V3 under the strictly-later rule (a later-date one could), and
  14:   one on the v2 wall would already be cleared by V4 (Grok 4.7; GPT-6 Astra's confirm corrected `forever');
  15: * moves nine rows `closed` -> `held` -- `sgirekills`, `sgirandomcolour`, `mapledmaaddr`, `xscaleinten`,
  16:   `ppcrldimimask`, `ppcrlwimiwidth`, `ppcgateimageskip`, `cxlaunchquotation`, `dashokclass` -- each keeping its closure
  17:   object as the record of the close, naming in `reopened` every commit whose subject called it closed (section L),
  18:   heading its state note with the warrant, and adding to its `hold_question` the packet of the pass Fable walled on;
  19: * adds `#565`'s two Fable stages to `wiringcliff`'s held work, with their question;
  20: * moves `fableheldform` `open` -> `held` (its own review is Fable's), with the design pass's seat entries;
  21: * FILES `untokenedanswers` (MED): the same defect for every seat and date -- a keyword correlate finds 497 matches among
  22:   entries counted as answers, on 129 rows, 81 closed, actual non-answers and known false positives together
  23:   (`regress/artifacts/fableheldform/design_20261018/CENSUS_wide.txt`, reconnaissance that GLM's finding motivated; its
  24:   own settling fact, a keyword-free review of every counted Fable entry, is owed there), including deliberate roster
  25:   exclusions that section H's nine-seat count reads as answers.  Not swept: that review, a forward-only check and an
  26:   owner ruling on how an excluded seat is recorded come first.
  27: 
  28: **Design pass 1** (`regress/artifacts/fableheldform/design_20261018/`): GPT-6 Astra, Grok 4.7 and GLM 5.3 all chose
  29: option A (tag in place, reopen to held).  Astra added option E -- an owner-authorized policy allowing a close with an
  30: explicitly deferred Fable review, changing section H and the state semantics together -- and ruled that only E needs
  31: the owner, the state correction being licensed by the ledger's own `_RETROACTIVE_OR_FORWARD_ONLY` semantics (`state` is
  32: a live field; correcting it rewrites no history); Grok agreed no fresh ruling is needed; GLM held that reopening
  33: committed closures is the owner's call and drafted the question.  **The owner question is recorded in
  34: `fableheldform`'s `hold_question`**: may a row close while its research or review question is held for Fable?  Until it
  35: is answered, rulings and commits proceed and closes wait.  Flags taken: the census's date cutoff missed
  36: `cxlaunchquotation`'s 2026-10-16 wall (Astra, GLM); `cxlaunchquotation` walled on V3 and V6 as well as V7 (all three);
  37: my brief said `ip30abortkill` "was committed held" while that commit was still in its hook (GLM); `ppcgateimageskip`'s
  38: review is 9/9 only through seven untokened non-answers -- five roster exclusions, GLM deliberately not fired, Fable
  39: held (Grok; the split is GPT-6 Astra's confirm).  Fable 5.1 walled (HTTP 429,
  40: `fable5_p1_WALL.txt`), held.  Confirm (GPT-6 Astra): 5 flags, all taken -- `ppcgateimageskip`'s packet is `packet_close527b_ASTRA.md` (as
  41: corrected by `527c`), not `527`; the keyword census is not GLM's keyword-free sweep, which stays owed; 497 are matches,
  42: not established non-answers; the seven notes on `ppcgateimageskip` are not all roster exclusions; `forever` overstated
  43: the discharge rule.  Fable 5.1 walled on the confirm too (`confirm/fable5_cf_WALL.txt`), held.  Opus 5.5, agy, kimi, deepseek and minimax deliberately not fired (the owner's
  44: 2026-10-17 roster).  `ledger.json`, `OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md`, `fable_queue.md`, `matrix.html` and this block only.
