    records: ip30abortkill's closure records -- clause (b) measured on the shipped 33-row instrument, 14/33 as named row by row before the run; the close is held for Fable, who walled on the closure check; its residuals and #560/#561's held src/ comments get rows
    
    #531 (686d179c, committed 2026-09-18) took four guest-reachable abort() calls out of
    dev_sgi_ip30.c; its 33-row detector, regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/ip30_abort_probe.py,
    runs in gate 14 since #566 (8faf4a16).  #566 left three things owed before the row could close:
    
    * clause (b), now measured (regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/close_20261018/): HEAD's dev_sgi_ip30.c
      with the removed fatal("IP30 legacy interrupt rewrite: TODO\n"); abort(); pair re-inserted
      verbatim at all four fixed sites scores 14/33 -- the six kill rows DEAD, thirteen state rows
      `died' -- and gate 14's block text reds 22 of its 41 checks on that log.  PREDICT_clause_b.txt,
      written before the build, named the same 19 reds (CLAUSE_B.txt keeps the file times);
    * the witness field now leads with the shipped instrument's pair (10/33 -> 33/33, #566's legs)
      and that leg; the 21-row pair and the 18-row order proof stay as history;
    * V7_nocounter (32/32, kill table 4) and the width axis V8_len4 (33/33, kill table 5), coverage
      debt, and the three questions #531's own CHANGELOG block filed and no row carried (the announce
      string's truth at arms that keep their stores, the per-instance latch axis, fall-through after
      a non-exiting fatal()) move to a new LOW row (Grok 4.7 dissenting for V7/V8, 2-1).
    
    The row does NOT close: Fable 5.1 was tried once and walled (HTTP 429, fable5_close531_WALL.txt),
    a row may not close while a stage awaits a seat, and the owner's 2026-10-17 directive holds
    Fable's stages with a question -- so ip30abortkill moves in work -> held, its hold_question
    carrying the closure review and the REGRESS measurement.  GPT-6 Astra's confirm overturned an
    interim draft that recorded the wall as a non-answer and closed the row.
    
    A second new LOW row carries 30 of the 37 corrections #560 and #561 HELD on 2026-10-06 (the 29
    src/ comments and one regress comment), which no ledger row carried; the other seven are
    hrecordowed's.  #561's places 7-10 -- dev_sgi_ip30.c's stale comment counts -- stay in that set.
    wiringcliff's commits field gains 8faf4a16.  No src/ is touched.
    
    Closure check: GPT-6 Astra 2 flags, Grok 4.7 3, GLM 5.3 (packet-fed) 5 -- adjudicated in the
    CHANGELOG block; confirm (GPT-6 Astra) 4 flags, all taken; micro-confirm 1 (a source path in
    this message that no hunk touches -- section C -- taken).  Fable 5.1 walled (held); Opus 5.5,
    agy, kimi, deepseek and minimax deliberately not fired (the owner's 2026-10-17 roster).
    
