48370:    "note": "*** MEASURED 2026-09-11, AND THE MEASUREMENT REFRAMED THE ROW. I FILED THIS AN HOUR AGO AS A\nSINGLE-FILE DEFECT WITH AN UNMEASURED POPULATION; THE CENSUS SAYS THE POPULATION IS 41 AND THAT\nEXITING 0 IS THE HOUSE IDIOM, NOT THE DEFECT. ***\n\nRaised by the GPT-6 Astra seat (unasked) about `ppc_rldicl_probe.py': *\"prints `SCORE', `FAILING',\nand its token without setting a failure exit status. Normal execution therefore exits successfully\neven with failed assertions.\"*  **That reading is CORRECT** -- its only `sys.exit(2)' is an\napparatus guard at `:89', not a failed-row path.  Cited: \nregress/artifacts/ppcrlwimiwidth/codex_detector_20260911.txt\n\nTHE DERIVER (run it; do not quote the numbers), against the WORKING TREE 2026-09-11:\n  for each regress/*_probe.py that prints a SCORE or _RESULT tally, take the text FROM the tally\n  onward and ask whether any `sys.exit'/`raise SystemExit' in it carries a nonzero status.\n\n    probes printing a SCORE/_RESULT tally : 67\n    exit status KEYED on the tally        : 26\n    exit ALWAYS 0 despite failed rows     : 41\n\n*** MY FIRST DERIVER RETURNED **3**, AND IT WAS WRONG FOR THE EXACT REASON THIS ROW'S OWN CLOSING\nPARAGRAPH WARNED AGAINST. ***  It asked *\"does the file contain a nonzero `sys.exit' anywhere?\"* --\na CORRELATE -- so `ppc_rldicl_probe.py' scored CLEAN on the strength of its apparatus guard, and\nthe subject of the finding was excluded from the census of the finding.  **Keyed on what defines\nthe class -- an exit keyed on the tally, searched only AFTER the tally is computed -- the answer is\n41.  Wrong by 13x.**  *The row telling the next person not to key on a correlate was filed with a\ncount derived from a correlate.*\n\n**SO THE DEFECT IS NOT THE 41. IT IS THE SPLIT.**  The house idiom in this tree is that a probe\nPRINTS result lines and the GATE greps them -- which is why no gate has ever been misled, and why\n41 probes exiting 0 has cost nothing.  But 26 probes do the opposite, several with the identical\n`sys.exit(0 if ok == len(rows) else 1)' shape.  **A gate author who has read those 26 reasonably\nconcludes that exit status is a supported channel, and wiring any of the 41 that way yields a check\nthat CANNOT FAIL** -- green whether or not every assertion failed.  That is the dangerous direction:\nit reassures.\n\n*** THE HOUSE IDIOM DOES NOT MERELY AVOID THE EXIT-STATUS CHANNEL -- IT **REFUSES** IT IN WRITING,\nAND I ONLY FOUND THAT BY OPENING THE GATES AFTER RECORDING `verified' FROM MEMORY. ***\n\n    gate_arm.sh:672          python3 arm_bdt_probe.py \"$PMAX\" > \"$BDTLOG\" 2>&1 || true\n    gate_arm.sh:674          if ! grep -q \"ARMBDT_RESULT=\" \"$BDTLOG\"; then        <- PARSE BEFORE SCORE\n    gate_arm.sh:687          check \"bdt rows run\"     \"$bwant\" 32                 <- denominator pinned\n    gate_arm.sh:688          check \"bdt rows correct\" \"$bgot\"  \"$bwant\"\n\n    gate_sh_rounding.sh:1457 python3 -u wdc_altdigin_probe.py ... > \"$ADLOG\" 2>&1 || true\n    gate_sh_rounding.sh:1459 if ! grep -q \"WDC_ALTDIGIN_RESULT=\" \"$ADLOG\"; then\n    gate_sh_rounding.sh:1485 check \"wdc_altdigin rows run\"     \"${adres#*/}\" 16\n    gate_sh_rounding.sh:1486 check \"wdc_altdigin rows correct\" \"${adres%/*}\" \"${adres#*/}\"\n\n**`|| true` is a DELIBERATE discard of rc, and the `grep -q ..._RESULT=` guard is what catches a\nprobe that crashed or printed nothing** -- so absence reds and a malformed result line cannot reach\nan empty-variable `check \"\" \"\"` that would pass.  Both halves are present in both gates.\n\n*That is the strongest available evidence for repair (1) below: the tree has already CHOSEN the\nresult-line channel, twice, explicitly.  The 41 probes that exit 0 are not 41 latent defects -- they\nare 41 probes following the channel the gates actually read.  The 26 that key exit on the tally are\nthe ones carrying an idiom no gate consumes.*\n\nNOT A LIVE DEFECT TODAY, verified: `arm_bdt_probe.py' and `wdc_altdigin_probe.py' are both in the\n41, and both of their gate sections grep RESULT LINES with pinned denominators (`bdt rows run' 32,\n`wdc_altdigin rows run' 16) rather than testing rc.  See [[armbdt]] and [[wdcaltdigin]].\n\nDISPOSITION QUESTION, unresolved and put to the adjudicating seat as Q-G2: `ppc_rldicl_probe.py'\nbelongs to the CLOSED `#522', so a change there is an L4 in a closed round, a MEASURED FALSE PASS\n(L2, follow-up commit), or a new filed row -- the late-dissent rule gives exactly those three.\n\nTHE REPAIR IS NOT `fix 41 probes'.  A sweep of that size is the `#392' shape and would be switched\noff.  The cheap forms, in order of cost: **(1)** every NEW gate section greps result lines, never\nrc -- which is already the practice; **(2)** a probe whose exit is keyed says so in its header, so\na reader can tell the idioms apart; **(3)** forward-only, a new probe picks ONE idiom and the\nround that adds it says which.  See [[ppcprobescorestale]], same file."
